SECTION 10 — BACKEND SETUP AND CHICKEN-EGG PROBLEM
================================================================

Problem:
  You need S3 bucket to store state file
  But Terraform uses state file to create S3 bucket
  You cannot do both in same terraform apply

Solution:
  Step 1: Create S3 bucket in SEPARATE folder (backend-setup/)
          This folder has its own terraform init and apply
          State is stored locally for this step only
          cd backend-setup/
          terraform init
          terraform apply

  Step 2: Now S3 bucket exists in AWS
          Add backend.tf to main project with bucket name
          Run terraform init in main project
          Terraform asks: copy state to S3? → yes
          From now on all state stored in S3

State locking with DynamoDB:
  Engineer 1 runs terraform apply
  → Terraform writes lock to DynamoDB
  Engineer 2 runs terraform apply at same time
  → Terraform sees lock → waits or fails with error
  Engineer 1 finishes → lock removed
  Engineer 2 can now proceed
  Result: state never corrupted


