SECTION 14 — DEPLOYMENT COMMANDS IN ORDER
================================================================

Step 1: Create key pair (run once before anything)
  aws ec2 create-key-pair \
    --key-name hasham-key \
    --query 'KeyMaterial' \
    --output text > ~/.ssh/hasham-key.pem
  chmod 400 ~/.ssh/hasham-key.pem

Step 2: Find your IP
  curl https://checkip.amazonaws.com
  Set result in terraform.tfvars as: my_ip = "YOUR.IP.HERE/32"

Step 3: Create remote backend
  cd backend-setup/
  terraform init
  terraform apply    → type yes

Step 4: Deploy main project
  cd ..
  terraform init     → type yes when asked to copy state to S3
  terraform plan     → review what will be created (~23 resources)
  terraform apply    → type yes, wait 3-5 minutes

Step 5: Get outputs
  terraform output
  terraform output bastion_ssh_command   → copy this command

Step 6: Test bastion
  ssh -i ~/.ssh/hasham-key.pem ubuntu@<bastion_public_ip>
  Inside bastion: hostname → shows ip-10-0-1-xxx (public subnet)

Step 7: Test NAT Gateway (from inside a private EC2)
  curl https://checkip.amazonaws.com
  → Returns NAT GW Elastic IP, not your laptop IP
  → Proves private EC2 → NAT GW → internet is working

Cleanup:
  terraform destroy
  cd backend-setup/ → remove prevent_destroy → terraform destroy


